================================================================================
Third-Party Software
================================================================================

This product depends on the following third-party software, which is
distributed under its respective license. None of these dependencies are
bundled into this repository; they are fetched at build time via CMake
FetchContent or linked from the system.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. OpenBLAS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Homepage : https://www.openblas.net/
   License  : BSD 3-Clause License (GPL v3 compatible)
   Use      : BLAS / LAPACK numerical routines (matrix products, SVD).
              Used in place of MKL to preserve GPL v3 compatibility
MKL is excluded because its
              proprietary Intel Simplified Software License is incompatible
              with GPL v3's strong copyleft.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. pybind11
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Homepage : https://github.com/pybind/pybind11
   License  : BSD 3-Clause License (GPL v3 compatible)
   Use : C++ ↔ Python bindings. Fetched via CMake FetchContent


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. NVIDIA CUDA Toolkit (optional)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Homepage : https://developer.nvidia.com/cuda-toolkit
   License  : NVIDIA Software License Agreement (proprietary; linked under
              the GPL v3 System Library Exception, GPL)
   Use      : GPU backend (FullState GPU, TensorNetwork GPU). Used via cuBLAS
              and cuSolver only — no cuTensorNet or cuQuantum dependency
Required only when QPLAYER_ENABLE_CUDA=ON;
              CPU-only builds do not link CUDA.

================================================================================
QASM Acceptance Test Vectors
================================================================================

The OpenQASM v2 test programs under `tests/data/qasm/` are derived from
the OpenQASM 2.0 examples and qelib1.inc, which are released by IBM under the
Apache License, Version 2.0 (Apache 2.0 → GPL v3 is one-way compatible per
the FSF compatibility matrix). See:

   https://github.com/openqasm/openqasm
   https://github.com/Qiskit/openqasm

================================================================================
Test Framework
================================================================================

The unit/integration test framework under `tests/framework/` is original code
written specifically for this project. No external test framework (GoogleTest,
Catch2, doctest, etc.) is used.
